#heading(level: 1, numbering: none)[Summary]

This fictional dissertation demonstrates how a full doctoral thesis can be
organized in Typst. It uses Marie Curie and other historic scientists as
deliberately playful placeholder names; it is not a historical reconstruction
or a statement about TU Delft affiliations. The chapters contain illustrative
text, equations, tables, figures, algorithms, code listings, and references so
that prospective users can judge the result before replacing it with their own
work.
